      {
        "text": "Frances Ann Hurley, a Democrat, is running for State Senator in the 18th District. She served in the Illinois House from 2013 to 2023. Prior to that, she was an aide to Chicago aldermen and director of the Saint Christina Manna Program. She chaired the House Police and Fire Committee. She sponsored legislation that became law regarding the special education maximum age and state police law enforcement. Her campaign says she co-chaired the First Responders Suicide Prevention Taskforce, which proposed mental health solutions for first responders. In 2019, as Human Services Committee chair, she halted bills pertaining to reproductive health care and abortion, Capitol News Illinois reported.",
